    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0515" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">870.811/205: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-01T13:00:00+02:00">September 1,
                            1940—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 1—12:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3844. My 3821, August 30, 4 p.m. The press today contains a DNB announcement that
                    on the invitation of the German Government <pb facs="0516" n="504"
                        xml:id="pg504"/> discussions by experts of the governments concerned will
                    take place in Vienna in the next few days on international Danubian
                        questions.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d532-f1"/> It is stated that the
                    International Danubian Commission at Belgrade set up by Versailles continued to
                    function with a French and British participation after the beginning of the war
                    but that this could no longer be tolerated in view of attempted enemy sabotage
                    of this important German supply route. The Vienna conference of experts it is
                    added is to set up a new provisional arrangement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d532-f1" n="1" xml:id="d532-f1-content">
                <p>The conference met September 5–12. No invitation was extended to the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
